+// Hands on the world (Ratchet's solid hands and fingers on the world, simplified): the palm, a sphere, moved from the
+// shoulder to the controller, stops where it meets the level or a solid object, so the hand rests on a wall instead of
+// going through; the fingers, a smaller sphere from the palm to their tips, curl over what is in front of them. Only
+// what is drawn moves: the controller's own path stays the gestures' and the punches'.
+constexpr float kPalmRadius = 0.05f, kFingerRadius = 0.02f, kFingerReach = 0.16f;  // game metres
+constexpr float kShoulderAside = 0.22f, kShoulderDown = 0.08f;                     // from the neck, game metres
+// The fingers over what they meet (0.1.1, the owner: "finger bending against environments isnt as smooth or responsive
+// as ... our openrac work"): as Ratchet's, they stop on a wall fast (kFingerStops) and let go of it slower
+// (kFingerFollows), so a probe that misses for a frame does not flick them open; each eased the more the farther it has
+// to go, not at one speed.
+constexpr float kFingerStops = 18.0f, kFingerFollows = 7.0f;  // of a full curl a second: out of a wall, around it
